    "TREATMENT": {
      "present": true,
      "status": "content",
      "content_blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "level": 0,
          "text": "surgical excision; survival >1.5 years with",
          "pdf_page": 1366,
          "printed_page": 1284,
          "column": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Pinna: complete pinnectomy.",
          "pdf_page": 1366,
          "printed_page": 1284,
          "column": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "level": 1,
          "text": "Appropriate surgical excision may require",
          "pdf_page": 1366,
          "printed_page": 1284,
          "column": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Ear canal tumors locally invasive (57–67%) pinnectomy and possibly vertical ear canal and can recur locally despite surgery; prognosis ablation; must remove lesion with margin is guarded. of normal tissue.",
          "pdf_page": 1366,
          "printed_page": 1284,
          "column": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Dogs—median survival 5.3 months with",
          "pdf_page": 1366,
          "printed_page": 1284,
          "column": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "level": 1,
          "text": "Alternatives include photodynamic",
          "pdf_page": 1366,
          "printed_page": 1284,
          "column": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "level": 0,
          "text": "bulla involvement compared to >58 months therapy (less predictable; multiple without. treatments may be required), cryosurgery",
          "pdf_page": 1366,
          "printed_page": 1284,
          "column": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Cats—median survival 3.8 months; worse (for small, superficial lesions), strontium prognosis with bulla involvement; median plesiotherapy (superficial radiation survival 1.5 months with neurologic signs. therapy), electrochemotherapy with bleomycin, or curettage/diathermy.",
          "pdf_page": 1366,
          "printed_page": 1284,
          "column": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Ear canal/middle ear:",
          "pdf_page": 1366,
          "printed_page": 1284,
          "column": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "level": 1,
          "text": "Total ear canal ablation and bulla",
